def privacy():
 return '''<section class="container page-intro"><div class="eyebrow">INFORMATION</div><h1>Privacy, clearly.</h1><p class="hero-intro">Information about this website and the current NexaTik desktop workflow.</p></section><article class="container prose"><h2>This website</h2><p>This site has no account-registration form, advertising scripts or analytics configured. It uses locally hosted interface images and styles. Hosting infrastructure may process routine connection data such as IP addresses and request logs.</p><h2>Downloads on GitHub</h2><p>Setup downloads open on GitHub. GitHub handles those download requests under its own privacy policy. This website does not ask for your GitHub password or a personal access token.</p><h2>The desktop application</h2><p>NexaTik saves selected videos, metadata, settings and history on your computer. It connects to selected content platforms to load metadata and download available media. Update checks contact the public NexaTik GitHub Releases endpoint.</p><h2>Browser verification</h2><p>Some profile scans open Chrome or Edge. In version 0.5.2, Instagram uses a dedicated local browser profile to reuse a session. If you log in, credentials belong on the platform's own browser page. Session access is used for the requested scan and subsequent metadata/download operations; browser and platform privacy policies also apply.</p><h2>Scope</h2><p>This describes the features configured in this release, not a guarantee about third-party platform or hosting behavior. Do not include passwords, session cookies or private account data in a support screenshot or report.</p></article>'''

def terms():
 return '''<section class="container page-intro"><div class="eyebrow">INFORMATION</div><h1>Use & download<br>information.</h1><p class="hero-intro">A few clear expectations before you download.</p></section><article class="container prose"><h2>Content permissions</h2><p>Only download content you own or are authorized to save, where permitted by the relevant platform. Access to a video does not itself grant copying or redistribution rights. NexaTik does not grant rights to third-party content or bypass private account permissions.</p><h2>Current availability</h2><p>The current NexaTik 0.5.2 release is free. A paid activation system or ten-video trial limit has not been added. NexaRemote and NexaConnect are product previews on this website; public downloads are not yet listed.</p><h2>Platform access and release limits</h2><p>Content platforms can change their interfaces, access rules and verification flows. Available videos, metadata and profile lists can vary. New browser routes are not a promise that every account or video will work.</p><h2>Installers and updates</h2><p>Use the complete installer from the linked NexaTik GitHub release. Finish active work before installing or updating. Keep your own copies of important videos and metadata. The application requires internet access for content requests and update checks.</p><h2>Independent software</h2><p>Nexa Software is not presented as affiliated with YouTube, Facebook, Instagram, TikTok, AnyDesk or TeamViewer. Their names identify platforms or other products and remain associated with their respective owners.</p></article>'''

